I for one would not keep coming back to this game if it had a save
feature.  It's the constant threat of total annihilation of hours of
work that makes the game exhilarating and fun.  Having to start over
naked on level 1 is simultaneously the greatest and most annoying part
of the game.  That and having your priest choke on a meatball on his
ascension run.  But this is exactly my point, I have fond memories of
my deaths, which would simply have been 'Oops, reload, forget' moments
with a save feature.

If you want to play with saving, by all means please do.  Just don't
come in here and say it's 'moral'.  There's no morality involved in
how you play a video game.  And don't claim it's not cheating, you are
manipulating the game externally.  There's nothing amoral about
cheating either, but are you really surprised that you posted a cheat
in a games newsgroup, called it moral, and got flamed for it?


